{
  "configuration_id": "config_049",
  "reason": "Evidence: The largest single improvement in this study came from switching the RNA encoder from pca_n2000 to scvi_n200 in the multimodal/multiprofile/ViT-L/avgpool/weighted setup (0.635 → 0.706, config_025→config_037), confirming that learned RNA encoders capture far more discriminative structure than PCA. However, scgpt—another learned single-cell RNA encoder with a different inductive bias (generative vs. variational)—has not been tested in any multimodal configuration. Uncertainty: It is unknown whether scgpt matches, exceeds, or falls short of scvi_n200 in this setting, and whether the ~7% gain from PCA→scvi generalizes to other learned encoders. This experiment (config_049: multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) slots scgpt into the exact best-performing architecture, isolating the RNA-encoder variable. Why best next: It directly tests the highest-leverage unexplored design choice (RNA encoder identity) within the already-validated optimal pipeline (multiprofile, ViT-L, avgpool, weighted), so the result will either reveal a new best configuration or confirm scvi_n200 as the preferred encoder—either outcome sharply narrows the remaining search space under a limited budget."
}

